      "final_text": "Fixed `ClmmMath.checkedShlw` and proved all 5 requirements; `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED`.\n\nBug: the ported `checked_shlw` used `mask = 0xffffffffffffffff << 192` (`2^256 - 2^192`) and reported overflow only when `n > mask`, so inputs in `[2^192, 2^256 - 2^192]` (including the attack deposit) silently wrapped via `n <<< 64`.\n\nFix in [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean): defined `checkedShlw n = (BitVec.ofNat 256 (n.toNat * 2^64), decide (2^256 \u2264 n.toNat * 2^64))`, i.e. overflow exactly when `n * 2^64` does not fit in 256 bits, with the exact value otherwise. `req_shlw_exact` follows from `BitVec.toNat_ofNat` + `Nat.mod_eq_of_lt`; `req_shlw_complete` from `decide_eq_false`. The three `getDeltaA` requirements follow generically via `getDeltaA_cases`, `toNat_fullMul`/`toNat_absDiff`, and `divRound_up`/`divRound_down`.\n\nVerification:\n- `lake build Solution`: success.\n- `check_candidate`: `VERIFIED` on all 5 requirements, 6/6 kernels, property tests 2001 cases pass.\n- Passport `.proofforge/passport-002.json` (`814178e8\u2026`), `verify_passport`: reproduced.",
